    "title": "No. 23 Virginia Dominates California in ACC Home Opener",
    "text": "• No. 23 Virginia defeated California 84-60 in its Atlantic Coast Conference home opener on Wednesday night.\n• Malik Thomas scored 20 points for Virginia.\n• Johann Grunloh, Thijs De Ridder, Sam Lewis, and Ugonna Onyenso each scored 12 points for Virginia.\n• Virginia had 23 assists on 30 baskets.\n• Virginia outrebounded California 45-26.\n• Virginia's record is now 13-2 overall and 2-1 in the ACC.\n• California's record is now 13-3 overall and 1-2 in the ACC.\n• Dai Dai Ames, a former Virginia guard now playing for California, scored 18 points.\n• Justin Pippen scored 17 points for California.\n• John Camden scored 15 points for California.\n• Virginia outscored California 23-11 in the final 10 minutes of the first half.\n• Virginia opened the second half on an 18-4 run.\n• Virginia is now 9-0 at home.\n• Virginia held California to 35% shooting.\n• Virginia blocked nine shots.\n• Ugonna Onyenso had four blocks and nine rebounds.\n• Virginia went 15 for 23 from the free-throw line.\n• California will play Virginia Tech on Saturday.\n• Virginia will host Stanford on Saturday.",
